Track 2: Työvuoro
- Story & Context: Named after the grueling sixteen-hour midnight shift, this track was recorded live during a real methane-gas lockdown in the lower drifts of the Pyhäsalmi mine. Cellist Katya played a single, suspended A-minor chord for three hours straight without taking a breath to keep the panic-stricken miners from breaking containment. As the air scrubbers hissed their rhythmic white noise, the miners began softly thumping their boot-heels against the iron floor grating in perfect neuro-syncopation. "Breath goes in as iron, but comes out soft like fog," she whispered into her bone-conduction microphone just before the backup generator died.
